{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a direct C-H oxidative difluoromethylation of various heterocycles using sodium difluoromethane sulfonate (Hu's reagent) as the radical precursor. The reaction is catalyzed by the organic dye Rose Bengal under visible light (green LEDs) with air (O2) as the terminal oxidant, avoiding the need for transition metals or stoichiometric chemical oxidants. The method was applied to late-stage functionalization of bioactive molecules, including the synthesis of F2TDR, which showed significant antitumor activity.",
